ng together four prime numbers: 2, 2, 2 and 3. How many primes must be multiplied to make 2400?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"fab1c4c52112c314f16203b0e2863edc4ef43958df7ddcc1f89bc7ef0e417d03"},"seconds":28.079163789749146,"seed":449447450745008726,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of determining how many prime numbers must be multiplied to make 2400, we start by finding the prime factorization of 2400.\n\nStep 1: Prime Factorization of 2400\n- First, notice that 2400 is an even number, which means it is divisible by 2:\n  \\[\n  2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  1200 \\div 2 = 600\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  600 \\div 2 = 300\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  300 \\div 2 = 150\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  150 \\div 2 = 75\n  \\]\n\n- Now, 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next prime number, which is 3:\n  \\[\n  75 \\div 3 = 25\n  \\]\n\n- Next, 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next prime number, which is 5:\n  \\[\n  25 \\div 5 = 5\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  5 \\div 5 = 1\n  \\]\n\nThus, the prime factorization of 2400 is:\n\\[\n2400 = 2^5 \\times 3 \\times 5^2\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Count the Number of Prime Factors\n- We count the total number of prime factors in the factorization:\n  \\[\n  2^5 \\times 3 \\times 5^2\n  \\]\n  - There are 5 factors of 2.\n  - There is 1 factor of 3.\n  - There are 2 factors of 5.\n\nAdding these together, the total number of prime factors is:\n\\[\n5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of prime numbers that must be multiplied to make 2400 is \\boxed{8}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
